      "files": {
        "18f6ef61-b149-4381-9ed5-f7139a40d197": {
          "id": "18f6ef61-b149-4381-9ed5-f7139a40d197",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Byte's Music Player</title>\n    <style>\n        body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif; margin: 20px; text-align: center; background-color: #1a1a2e; color: #e0e0e0; }\n        h1 { color: #e94560; margin-bottom: 20px; }\n        p { margin-bottom: 25px; font-size: 1.1em; }\n        .console-hint { background-color: #0f3460; padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px; display: inline-block; margin-top: 20px; font-size: 0.9em; }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <h1>Byte's Music Player</h1>\n    <p>Help Byte organize your music library by defining some song details. Open the console to see the song info!</p>\n    <div class=\"console-hint\">Remember to open your browser's console (F12) to see output from `script.js`.</div>\n\n    <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
          "folderId": "0",
          "type": "starter",
          "active": true
        },
        "dc1289f7-7ee7-4a4d-a439-68bb87dbfadb": {
          "id": "dc1289f7-7ee7-4a4d-a439-68bb87dbfadb",
          "name": "script.js",
          "contents": "// Welcome to Byte's Music Player!\n// We need to tell Byte about the songs in your library.\n\n// Your task: Create two variables for a song.\n\n// 1. Create a variable called `song_title`.\n//    This variable should store a String value, like \"Bohemian Rhapsody\" or \"Eye of the Tiger\".\n//    Example: let song_title = \"Sweet Child o' Mine\";\n\n// 2. Create a variable called `duration_seconds`.\n//    This variable should store an Integer (whole number) value, representing the song's length in seconds.\n//    Example: let duration_seconds = 368;\n\n// Write your code below this line:\n// --- Your code starts here ---\n\n\n// --- Your code ends here ---\n\n// Let's check the song details!\nconsole.log(\"--- Song Details ---\");\nconsole.log(\"Title: \" + song_title);\nconsole.log(\"Duration: \" + duration_seconds + \" seconds\");\nconsole.log(\"---------------------\");\n\n// If you see 'undefined' or an error, double-check that you've created both variables correctly.\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "type": "starter",
          "active": false
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "18f6ef61-b149-4381-9ed5-f7139a40d197",
        "dc1289f7-7ee7-4a4d-a439-68bb87dbfadb"
      ]
    },
    "long_instructions": "Welcome to Byte's Music Player! Byte is ready to organize your favorite tunes, but first, it needs to know some details about the songs.\r\n\r\nIn this level, you'll continue practicing creating variables, which are essential for storing information in your programs.\r\n\r\n1.  **Open `script.js`.** Inside this file, you'll find comments guiding you on what to add.\r\n2.  **Create a variable named `song_title`.** This variable should store a **String** (text) value, like `\"Bohemian Rhapsody\"` or `\"Eye of the Tiger\"`. Remember to put your chosen song title inside double quotes!\r\n3.  **Create a variable named `duration_seconds`.** This variable should store an **Integer** (whole number) value, representing the song's length in seconds, like `367` or `240`. This should be a number without quotes.\r\n4.  **Save `script.js`** and refresh `index.html` in your browser. Open your browser's console (usually by pressing `F12` or right-clicking and selecting \"Inspect\" then \"Console\") to see if your song's details are displayed correctly. Byte will print out the values you assigned!",
    "generate_outline": "Scenario: The Music Player\r\n\r\nTask: Create variables for song_title (String) and duration_seconds (Integer)."
